[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m The "stars and bars" theorem states that the number of ways to distribute \( n \) indistinguishable objects into \( k \) distinguishable bins is given by the binomial coefficient \( \binom{n+k-1}{k-1} \).
