[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, the resulting shape is an isosceles right triangle. In an isosceles right triangle, the legs are congruent, and the hypotenuse is \(\sqrt{2}\) times the length of each leg. Let the length of each leg be \(x\). The area of the triangle is given by:
