[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m [response] To determine how many pots have three different colored balloons attached, we need to find the number of pots that are multiples of 4, 6, and 10. This is because a pot will have three different colored balloons if it is a multiple of 4, 6, and 10. The least common multiple (LCM) of 4, 6, and 10 will give us the number of pots that have three different colored balloons.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m First, we find the LCM of 4, 6, and 10. The prime factorizations are:
