[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m The volume \(V\) of a sphere is given by the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \[ V = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m where \(r\) is the radius of the sphere. We are given that the volume of the sphere is \(\frac{\pi}{6}\) cubic inches. So, we can set up the equation:
