[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m Substituting the given values, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 8 \times 112 = m \times n \implies 896 = m \times n
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m Since the GCD of \(m\) and \(n\) is 8, we can express \(m\) and \(n\) as \(m = 8a\) and \(n = 8b\) where \(a\) and \(b\) are coprime (i.e., \(\text{GCD}(a, b) = 1\)). Substituting these into the equation \(m \times n = 896\), we get:
