[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m [response] To determine the probability that the game will be won before the fourth turn, we need to consider the probability of winning on each turn and the probability of not winning on each turn. The probability of winning on any given turn is the probability of rolling a 1 or a 6 on the die and getting heads on the coin, which is \(\frac{2}{6} \times \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{6}\). The probability of not winning on any given turn is \(1 - \frac{1}{6} = \frac{5}{6}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m The game will be won before the fourth turn if the player wins on the first, second, or third turn. We can calculate this as follows:
