[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m So, the largest three-digit number divisible by 13 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \[ 13 \times 76 = 988 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m The sequence of three-digit numbers divisible by 13 is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \(a = 117\), the common difference \(d = 13\), and the last term \(l = 988\). The number of terms \(n\) in this sequence can be found using the formula for the \(n\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \]
