[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, the resulting shape is an isosceles right triangle with legs equal to the side length of the square, which is 7 inches. The hypotenuse of this triangle is the diagonal of the square, which can be calculated using the Pythagorean theorem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \text{Diagonal} = \sqrt{7^2 + 7^2} = \sqrt{49 + 49} = \sqrt{98} = 7\sqrt{2} \text{ inches}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m This diagonal is also the side length of the original square, confirming our calculation.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m The two congruent triangles formed are right triangles with legs of 7 inches each. The perimeter of one of these triangles is the sum of its three sides:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m 7 + 7 + 7\sqrt{2} = 14 + 7\sqrt{2}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=24255)[0m Thus, the number of inches in the perimeter of one of these triangles is \(\boxed{14 + 7\sqrt{2}}\).
